@startuml
title The minterm partition as a dispatch table (D'Antoni and Veanes)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam card {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

rectangle "channel c receiver predicates\n{ φ1, φ2, φ3 }   (T1 / T2, non-Z3)" as PREDS #DBEAFE

card "compute_minterms\nmaximal satisfiable\nsign-vector conjunctions" as CM #FEF3C7

rectangle "minterm cells — they partition the message domain" as CELLS #FEF3C7 {
  card "φ1 ∧ φ2 ∧ ¬φ3\n->  { C1, C2 }" as M1 #FEF9C3
  card "¬φ1 ∧ φ2 ∧ φ3\n->  { C2, C3 }" as M2 #FEF9C3
  card "¬φ1 ∧ ¬φ2 ∧ ¬φ3\n->  { }  (rests)" as M3 #FEF9C3
}

rectangle "message m\nclassified once into\nexactly one cell" as MSG #DCFCE7
rectangle "accepting contracts\n(dispatch result)" as OUT #DCFCE7

PREDS --> CM
CM --> CELLS : is_satisfiable prunes\nunrealizable cells
MSG --> M1 : evaluate distinguishing\natoms (decision DAG)
M1 --> OUT

note bottom of CELLS
  "All elements in the same minterm are treated identically
  by every predicate" — so a cell names exactly which
  contracts accept m. Worst case 2^N cells; build it
  per channel and lazily.
end note

legend right
|= Color |= Role |
|<#DBEAFE> | input predicate set |
|<#FEF3C7> | minterm construction / cells |
|<#DCFCE7> | message classification + result |
endlegend
@enduml
